        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Wasn\u2019t I just saying that <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/3120296/flat-rate-ai-plans-are-broken-blame-ai-agents.html\">flat-rate AI plans are broken</a>? Now we\u2019ve got more proof, this time coming from the makers of Claude.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Eagled-eyed Claude users caught Anthropic tinkering with the signup page for individual Claude Pro and Max plans. Specifically, they saw that <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/ClaudeAI/comments/1ss3asp/does_claudes_20_plan_no_longer_include_claude_code/\">Claude Code was nixed</a> from the features available on Claude Pro.\u00a0</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Claude Code bullet point eventually returned to the Claude Pro signup page, and <a href=\"https://x.com/TheAmolAvasare/status/2046724659039932830\">Anthropic Head of Growth Amol Avasare later posted on social media</a> that the change was just \u201ca small test on ~2% of new prosumer signups,\u201d",
